Z||000000||Philphine||07-26-2001||03:48 PM||||<BR>barring some surprise repair, what do i need to get as part of a head gasket replacement? i know the gasket itself and i've heard new head bolts (studs?), more oil and anti-freeze. what else? also, would it be better to try and get the head off another '84 i have (both cars '84) have whatever work you have done on a head during changing done and just swap heads during the gasket change? what kind of money are we talkin'? <P>i need to catch up on my repairs before i find another fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||07-26-2001||04:59 PM||||plan on some exhaust manifold problems. if youve never had it off. stud kit, exhaust gasket (Felpro).||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-26-2001||05:02 PM||||When I did the head gasket on my 84, I also changed the...<P>-valve springs<BR>-valve seals<BR>-temp sensor<BR>-cooling fan switch<BR>-pushrods<BR>-rocker arms<BR>-lifters<BR>-head bolts<P>The seals come with the head gasket set, and the other stuff added up to a total of like $150 or so.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||07-26-2001||07:37 PM||||the head bolts have to go. The originals are known weak. Don't be suprised if one or more exhaust side ones break or are alerady broken.||||reg||1
